IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulations 15 to 20 and 23: assigning a Social Insurance
-- Number (15), the documents the Minister may call for to establish a relationship (16, 17), the evidence of age and identity (18,
-- 18.1, 19), the statement of residence a person must give (20) and the Minister's powers to ask for more and to investigate (23).
--
-- Almost every provision here says what the Minister "may" do or what a person "shall" provide. Each is encoded as a rule answering
-- whether the power or the duty exists on the facts given; no rule here makes the Minister act. What the Minister is "satisfied" of,
-- or has "reasonable grounds" to believe, is a plain input: the text hands the judgment to the Minister and gives no test.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Assignment of Social Insurance Numbers to Applicants, Beneficiaries, Spouses or Common-law Partners`

-- src:125 | 15 Where a Social Insurance Number has not been assigned to an applicant or beneficiary or to the spouse or common-law partner of an applicant or beneficiary, the Minister may assign or cause to be assigned a Social Insurance Number to the applicant or beneficiary or to the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 15 (src:125)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has not been assigned to the applicant or beneficiary, or to the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15: the Minister may assign or cause to be assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a Social Insurance Number has not been assigned to the applicant or beneficiary, or to the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary` MEANS
    `a Social Insurance Number has not been assigned to the applicant or beneficiary, or to the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary`

§§ `Relationship Evidence`

-- 16(1): where information in support of the application needed to determine the relationship has not been received, the Minister may
-- require one of the documents named for that kind of relationship: for spouses (a), for common-law partners (b).
DECLARE `reg 16(1): Relationship between the applicant and the other person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 16(1)(a): spouses`
    `reg 16(1)(b): common-law partners`

DECLARE `reg 16(1): Document the Minister may require` IS ONE OF
    `reg 16(1)(a): a certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of the act of marriage`
    `reg 16(1)(b): a statutory declaration setting out information as to the relationship or, if applicable, any other evidence of the relationship`

-- src:128 | 16 (1) If the Minister has not received information in support of an application for a benefit that is necessary to determine the relationship between the applicant and their spouse or common-law partner, the Minister may require that one of the following documents be submitted:
-- src:129 | (a) in the case of spouses, their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage; or
-- src:130 | (b) in the case of common-law partners, a statutory declaration setting out information as to their relationship or, if applicable, any other evidence of the relationship.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 16(1) (src:128-130)
GIVEN `the Minister has not received information in support of the application for a benefit that is necessary to determine the relationship between the applicant and the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship` IS A `reg 16(1): Relationship between the applicant and the other person`
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 16(1): Document the Minister may require`
`reg 16(1): the document of which the Minister may require submission` `the Minister has not received information in support of the application for a benefit that is necessary to determine the relationship between the applicant and the other person` `the relationship` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has not received information in support of the application for a benefit that is necessary to determine the relationship between the applicant and the other person`
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER `the relationship`
               WHEN `reg 16(1)(a): spouses` THEN `reg 16(1)(a): a certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of the act of marriage`
               WHEN `reg 16(1)(b): common-law partners` THEN `reg 16(1)(b): a statutory declaration setting out information as to the relationship or, if applicable, any other evidence of the relationship`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:131 | (2) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the Minister may require that the original certificate of marriage or, if applicable, a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority be submitted.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 16(2) (src:131)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(2): the Minister may require the original certificate of marriage or, if applicable, a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority` `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage`

-- src:132 | (3) If there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available, the Minister may determine the relationship between the applicant and their spouse on the basis of a statutory declaration setting out information as to their marriage or, if applicable, any other evidence of the marriage.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 16(3) (src:132)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(3): the Minister may determine the relationship on the basis of a statutory declaration or other evidence of the marriage` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available`

-- 17: where the Minister lacks the evidence to decide whether a person for whom the supplement application requirement was waived has
-- a spouse or common-law partner, the Minister may use that person's tax return for the most recent calendar year for which the
-- filing due date has passed. Which year that is depends on the filing due date, which the Income Tax Act sets and the Regulations
-- do not state; it arrives as an input (fork F-17 in NOTES.md also takes "has passed" to mean the question day is later than it).
-- src:133 | 17 If the Minister does not have sufficient evidence or information to determine if a person, for whom the requirement for an application for a supplement has been waived under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act, has a spouse or common-law partner, the Minister may use the tax return filed with the Minister of National Revenue by that person for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed to make that determination.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 17 (src:133)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application for a supplement has been waived in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 11(3.1) of the Act (piece oa1)
      `the Minister does not have sufficient evidence or information to determine whether the person has a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 17: the Minister may use the person's tax return filed with the Minister of National Revenue` `the requirement for an application for a supplement has been waived in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act` `the Minister does not have sufficient evidence or information to determine whether the person has a spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
        `the requirement for an application for a supplement has been waived in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act`
    AND `the Minister does not have sufficient evidence or information to determine whether the person has a spouse or common-law partner`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 17 (src:133)
GIVEN `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the filing due date of the income tax return for the calendar year before the one in which the question is asked` IS A DATE -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 17: the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed` `the day on which the question is asked` `the filing due date of the income tax return for the calendar year before the one in which the question is asked` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the filing due date of the income tax return for the calendar year before the one in which the question is asked`
    THEN (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the question is asked`) MINUS 1
    ELSE (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the question is asked`) MINUS 2

§§ `Evidence of Age and Identity`

-- 18(1): "Subject to subsections (2) to (4) and section 19", the Minister must determine an applicant's age and identity on the basis
-- of (a) a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth, or (b) information made available by the Canada Employment
-- Insurance Commission. The rule answers whether either basis is at hand; the "subject to" provisions are the rules that follow.
-- src:136 | 18 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (4) and section 19, the Minister must determine an applicant’s age and identity for the purposes of the Act on the basis of
-- src:137 | (a) a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth; or
-- src:138 | (b) any information made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18(1) (src:136-138)
GIVEN `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information has been made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(1): the Minister can determine the applicant's age and identity on the basis of paragraph (a) or (b)` `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available` `information has been made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` MEANS
        `a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth is available`
    OR  `information has been made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

-- src:139 | (2) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth referred to in paragraph (1)(a), the Minister may require that the original birth certificate or, if applicable, a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority be submitted.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18(2) (src:139)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(2): the Minister may require the original birth certificate or, if applicable, a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority` `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a birth certificate or act of birth`

-- src:140 | (3) If there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available, the Minister may determine the applicant’s age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence respecting the applicant’s age and identity.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18(3) (src:140)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(3): the Minister may determine the applicant's age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents referred to in paragraph (1)(a) are available`

-- 18(4): the Minister may "if possible" use Statistics Canada's information when unable to determine age and identity under any of (1)
-- to (3). Whether it is possible is the second input.
-- src:141 | (4) If the Minister is unable to determine the applicant’s age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3), the Minister may, if possible, determine them on the basis of any information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 6 of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18(4) (src:141)
GIVEN `the Minister is unable to determine the applicant's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 6 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(4): the Minister may determine the applicant's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada` `the Minister is unable to determine the applicant's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)` `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 6 of the Act` MEANS
        `the Minister is unable to determine the applicant's age and identity under any of subsections (1) to (3)`
    AND `it is possible to determine them on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 6 of the Act`

-- 18.1: the conditions for section 6 of the Act. (a) the request is in the form the Chief Statistician prescribes, bears the signed consent
-- of the person it concerns and includes the specific information needed to search the census records; and (b) what Statistics Canada
-- supplies is kept confidential and not used for any purpose other than determining the applicant's age as the Act or the Canada Pension
-- Plan requires.
-- src:142 | 18.1 For the purposes of section 6 of the Act, the conditions are the following:
-- src:143 | (a) the request to Statistics Canada must
-- src:144 | (i) be made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician of Canada,
-- src:145 | (ii) bear the signed consent of the person who is the subject of the request, and
-- src:146 | (iii) include the specific information that is necessary for searching the census records; and
-- src:147 | (b) any information supplied by Statistics Canada must be kept confidential and must not be used for a purpose other than determining the applicant’s age as required under the Act or the Canada Pension Plan, as the case may be.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18.1(a) (src:142-146)
GIVEN `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request bears the signed consent of the person who is the subject of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request includes the specific information that is necessary for searching the census records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18.1(a): the request to Statistics Canada meets the conditions` `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician of Canada` `the request bears the signed consent of the person who is the subject of the request` `the request includes the specific information that is necessary for searching the census records` MEANS
        `the request is made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician of Canada`
    AND `the request bears the signed consent of the person who is the subject of the request`
    AND `the request includes the specific information that is necessary for searching the census records`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18.1(b) (src:147)
GIVEN `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is kept confidential` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is used for a purpose other than determining the applicant's age as required under the Act or the Canada Pension Plan, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18.1(b): the information supplied by Statistics Canada is handled as the condition requires` `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is kept confidential` `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is used for a purpose other than determining the applicant's age as required under the Act or the Canada Pension Plan, as the case may be` MEANS
        `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is kept confidential`
    AND (NOT `the information supplied by Statistics Canada is used for a purpose other than determining the applicant's age as required under the Act or the Canada Pension Plan, as the case may be`)

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 18.1 (src:142-147)
GIVEN `the request to Statistics Canada meets the conditions of paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information supplied is handled as paragraph (b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18.1: the conditions for the purposes of section 6 of the Act are met` `the request to Statistics Canada meets the conditions of paragraph (a)` `the information supplied is handled as paragraph (b) requires` MEANS
        `the request to Statistics Canada meets the conditions of paragraph (a)`
    AND `the information supplied is handled as paragraph (b) requires`

-- src:148 | 19 Where the age of an applicant has been determined under the Canada Pension Plan, that determination may be accepted by the Minister for the purposes of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 19 (src:148)
GIVEN `the age of the applicant has been determined under the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19: the Minister may accept the determination of the applicant's age made under the Canada Pension Plan` `the age of the applicant has been determined under the Canada Pension Plan` MEANS
    `the age of the applicant has been determined under the Canada Pension Plan`

§§ `Residence`

-- 20(2): "Unless the Minister requires otherwise under the Act", a person need not provide the statement in the circumstances set out in
-- sections 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act. Those circumstances are decided by the Act, so they are one input.
-- src:153 | (2) Unless the Minister requires otherwise under the Act, a person is not required to provide a statement under subsection (1) in the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 20(2) (src:153)
GIVEN `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 5, 11, 19 and 21 of the Act (piece oa1)
      `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 20(2): the person is not required to provide a statement under subsection (1)` `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist` `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act` MEANS
        `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist`
    AND (NOT `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act`)

-- 20(1): to enable the Minister to determine eligibility in respect of residence, the person or someone acting for the person shall
-- provide a statement giving full particulars of all periods of residence in Canada and all absences relevant to eligibility.
-- src:152 | 20 (1) To enable the Minister to determine a person’s eligibility in respect of residence in Canada, the person or someone acting on the person’s behalf shall provide a statement giving full particulars of all periods of residence in Canada and of all absences from Canada that are relevant to that eligibility.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 20(1) (src:152)
GIVEN `the Minister is determining the person's eligibility in respect of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 20(1): the person or someone acting on the person's behalf must provide a statement giving full particulars of all periods of residence in Canada and of all absences from Canada that are relevant to that eligibility` `the Minister is determining the person's eligibility in respect of residence in Canada` `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist` `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act` MEANS
        `the Minister is determining the person's eligibility in respect of residence in Canada`
    AND (NOT (`reg 20(2): the person is not required to provide a statement under subsection (1)` `the circumstances set out in subsection 5(2) or (5), 11(3) or (4), 19(4.1) or 21(5) or (5.1) of the Act exist` `the Minister requires otherwise under the Act`))

§§ `Further Information and Investigation Before or After the Approval of an Application or Before or After the Requirement of an Application Is Waived`

-- 23(1): at any time before or after approval of an application, or after the requirement for an application is waived, the Minister may
-- require the applicant, the person who applied on the applicant's behalf, the beneficiary or the person who receives payment on the
-- applicant's behalf, "as the case may be", to make available further information or evidence regarding eligibility. The text sets no
-- other condition and no time, so the only facts are who the person is.
-- src:257 | 23 (1) The Minister, at any time before or after approval of an application or after the requirement for an application is waived, may require the applicant, the person who applied on the applicant’s behalf, the beneficiary or the person who receives payment on the applicant’s behalf, as the case may be, to make available or allow to be made available further information or evidence regarding the eligibility of the applicant or the beneficiary for a benefit.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 23(1) (src:257)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person who applied on the applicant's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person who receives payment on the applicant's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(1): the Minister may require the person to make available or allow to be made available further information or evidence regarding the eligibility of the applicant or the beneficiary for a benefit` `the person is the applicant` `the person is the person who applied on the applicant's behalf` `the person is the beneficiary` `the person is the person who receives payment on the applicant's behalf` MEANS
        `the person is the applicant`
    OR  `the person is the person who applied on the applicant's behalf`
    OR  `the person is the beneficiary`
    OR  `the person is the person who receives payment on the applicant's behalf`

-- 23(2): the Minister may at any time investigate the eligibility of a person to receive a benefit, including the capacity of a beneficiary
-- to manage his own affairs. The text names no condition at all, so the rule has no input and says so.
-- src:258 | (2) The Minister may at any time make an investigation into the eligibility of a person to receive a benefit including the capacity of a beneficiary to manage his own affairs.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 23(2) (src:258)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(2): the Minister may at any time make an investigation into the eligibility of a person to receive a benefit` MEANS
    TRUE
